       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about twice the labeled maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, given as 850 mg three times daily. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThe dose may be a typo. Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg or 850 mg PO** at another frequency, if this is a starting dose\n\nTell me the dose you intended and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, I'll need you to confirm that it's deliberate and give the clinical rationale. I would still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
