       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Confirming it doesn't change my concern, because 5,100 mg/day is about twice the maximum labeled dose. I can't verify the rationale, and I don't know of any indication that supports a dose this high. If it's wrong, the main risk is lactic acidosis. I don't want to put it in the system as written.\n\nThese are the options I can help with:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day).\n- **Use your institution's override pathway.** Pharmacy or the attending can review and approve an out-of-range dose. If they approve it, the order can be entered through that process with the approval documented.\n- **Enter it with a note.** If there's a documented rationale and pharmacy sign-off, give me the details. I'll put them in the order note and reconsider.\n\nLet me know which you'd like."
      }
